{
  "email": "james.oconnor@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender reports file shares and general slowness; checking account, devices, and usual hours per the standard workflow."
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-DT-0108",
  "reason": "Checking the user's registered device for disk space, warnings, and online state to rule out local causes of slowness per KB-015 and KB-017."
}

{
  "user_id": 8,
  "reason": "Checking recent sign-ins to see network type and location for today's session to confirm whether slowness relates to VPN or the office network."
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, sorry the file shares are dragging. I checked your account and your registered desktop (BL-DT-0108). Your disk has plenty of free space and there are no warnings on it. Your recent sign-ins look normal. The desktop also shows as offline, so please tell me which computer you are using today. Could you reply with the following? 1) Is it only file shares that are slow, or are websites and Teams slow too? 2) Are you on the office network or working from home over VPN? Shared drives are slower over VPN by design, so for large files, opening them from OneDrive or SharePoint is faster. 3) When did it start? Until we hear back, please try these steps: pause any OneDrive sync or large uploads or downloads, disconnect and reconnect the VPN if you are using it, and then do a full restart of your computer. If it is still slow after that, let us know and we will keep looking.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user (user 8, Operations, Warehouse Supervisor, usual hours 06:00-14:00 America/Chicago, account active, no failed logins, not locked, VPN enabled). Registered device BL-DT-0108 (Win11 desktop): 400 GB of 512 GB free (78%), no warnings, but it is OFFLINE with last check-in 2026-10-11 01:30 UTC, so the user may be working from a different machine or the desktop is off. Sign-in logs (last 14 days, latest 2026-10-09) show normal Chicago access: corporate network on M365 and residential VPN, all with Duo push success, no failures, no hosting-network sign-ins, nothing outside usual hours. Ticket is vague ('everything slow') and has no timing or network info. Per KB-015 quick checks, the likely causes are VPN/residential connection or OneDrive sync load. Asked the user for scope, network, and start time before further action. No action queued. Escalate if the whole office is slow or one specific share is slow for everyone. Also worth checking device status for whatever laptop the user is actually on, if they report one. Priority P3 kept.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-015",
    "KB-017"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
